{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’ve been vomiting since yesterday afternoon. I tried Ativan at home but it didn’t help. I just couldn’t stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And how are you feeling now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous. I feel shaky too. My blood sugar was 430 when I got here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your labs show high blood sugar and an acid imbalance, called ketoacidosis. We’re giving you insulin and fluids through your port to correct that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay… I’ve had this before. Is it bad this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s serious, but we’re treating it. Your anion gap was 28, which is high, but it’s already coming down with treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood pressure? It’s always high when I’m sick like this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was 216 over 112 when you arrived, and your heart rate was fast. That’s why we admitted you to the ICU for close monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m sorry… I know I’ve been here a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-04-26 02:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Your history shows this is often linked to your gastroparesis and anxiety. We’re treating both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-04-26 03:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood work shows your acid levels are improving. The insulin is working."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-04-26 03:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I still feel sick to my stomach though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-04-26 03:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re giving you Reglan and Zofran for nausea. You’re also getting IV fluids to stay hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your glucose is now 275, and your anion gap is down to 17. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning… Is the vomiting from my diabetes or my stomach not emptying?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s likely both. Your gastroparesis means your stomach empties slowly, and when your sugars are high, it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the anxiety? I know it makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, anxiety can trigger or worsen nausea. Psychiatry reviewed your case and recommended switching from Ativan to Klonopin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Why the change?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Klonopin may help with both anxiety and nausea long-term and has a lower risk of dependence. We’ll start it today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try it. I haven’t been great about seeing my psychiatrist, I know."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-04-26 06:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s okay. The important thing is you’re here now. We’ll help you set up follow-up before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well overnight. You kept down a popsicle yesterday, and your nausea seems better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I haven’t vomited since last night. That’s a relief."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re going to try advancing your diet to clear liquids today, then maybe soft foods tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I eat regular food soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll take it step by step. If you tolerate the liquids, we’ll move forward. Your blood sugar needs to stay stable too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars have been all over the place. I took my usual Lantus dose at home, but it didn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s common during flares. We gave you extra Humalog—35 units so far—and your sugars are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to adjust my insulin at home too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-04-27 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll continue your sliding scale with Humalog. We’ll make sure you have clear instructions before discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-04-27 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your latest labs look good. Glucose is 130, and your electrolytes are balanced. The alkalosis has resolved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-04-27 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my blood pressure?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-04-27 12:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s still a bit high when you’re nauseous, but we switched you to captopril for now. You’ll go back to lisinopril at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-04-27 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m glad things are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. You’re eating a regular diet now and haven’t vomited in over 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better. Can I go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re planning to discharge you today. You’ll stop Ativan and start Klonopin twice a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I need to see a psychiatrist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, within a month, to continue the Klonopin. We also recommend following up with your diabetes team and PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t have a PCP right now… I was let go from my clinic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. We’ll help you find a new provider. Your health is important, and we want to support you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I really want to do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We believe in you. Keep taking your medications, eat small meals, and reach out if nausea returns early."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And if I feel anxious, I should take the Klonopin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s meant to help prevent the cycle of anxiety and vomiting. Don’t wait until you’re very sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. Thank you for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll have your discharge papers ready soon, and a nurse will go over your meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-04-28 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready to go home and take care of myself better."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-04-26 02:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-04-28 16:20:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, gastroparesis, and a history of anxiety was admitted for severe nausea and vomiting, uncontrolled blood glucose, and hypertensive urgency. She presented with diabetic ketoacidosis and metabolic alkalosis, requiring IV insulin, fluids, and antiemetics. Her condition improved with treatment, and she transitioned to a regular diet. Psychiatry recommended switching from Ativan to Klonopin for better long-term management of anxiety-related nausea. She was discharged home in stable condition with medication changes and follow-up plans for psychiatry and diabetes care.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Alkalosis",
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Personal history of infections of the central nervous system"
    ]
  }
}
